Z||000000||Greg Piet||09-14-1999||12:48 AM||||Ok when launching at the christmas tree, what rpm do others take off at?<BR>Im running a v-6 4 speed isuzu.<BR>I just put on 4 new yokohama's, but I seem to spin them at about 2000 rpm's.  Im thinking i may just be too fast on the clutch, but I havent had this problem on other cars ||||reg||4
Z||000001||Cooter||09-14-1999||09:37 PM||||Try launching at different rpms and try not to ignite the tires. In my rear drive vehicles, I launch at about 3000 and at half throttle. As soon as the car starts to get traction, step into the throttle smoothly. Some fuel injected vehicles dont like a sudden jump from idle to full throttle for some reason. Something an old timer told me after watching my pathetic dragstrip performance was to be sure to "clear the engine" after coming into the prestage lights- rev the engine pretty good to clear anything that may have built up while idling in the staging area. This is really important if you do a burn-out because the hard acceleration in the water box and then coming to a quick stop may cause the engine to load up with fuel. Just dont float the lifters or oil down the track!||||reg||14
